    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-1999-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "At \\(10\\) o’clock, we have that the hour hand is at \\(10\\) and the minute hand is at \\(12.\\)\n\nThis means that the hands are a \\(\\frac{1}{6}\\) of the entire circle apart. This is equal to \\[ 360^{\\circ} \\cdot \\dfrac{1}{6} = 60^{\\circ}. \\]\n\nThus, C is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Each hour mark is \\(30^\\circ\\) apart",
        "At \\(10\\) o’clock, the hands are two hour marks apart"
      ],
